  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free in the bz2 and lzma decompressors after\n     a MemoryError\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-6100.patch: clear bzs->next_in and\n       lzs->next_in on both failure exits of decompress() in\n       Modules/_bz2module.c and Modules/_lzmamodule.c, the error label and\n       the decompress_buf() failure return, so a BZ2Decompressor or\n       LZMADecompressor reused after a failed input-buffer allocation or a\n       corrupt stream no longer reads or writes through a stale pointer\n       into the caller's released buffer\n     - CVE-2026-6100",
